;
; DEED clause profile: the six verb descriptiles, v1.0.0 (DRAFT)
; Prose and rationale: docs/estate-reconciliation/A7-contractiles-descriptiles-anchor.adoc
; sections 7.1 (files and the affirmation members), 7.3 (the verb
; descriptiles) and 8.5 (Bust grades); rulings W3, W8, J4, J5, J14, J20 and
; A2 D2. M3 module order: section 11.
;
; A CLAUSE PROFILE, not a new grammar. Every rule below is also a `clause` or
; `field` of deed.abnf v1.5.0, so a verb descriptile still passes deed_lint
; unchanged. Rules it borrows: string, value, symbol and token-sep are
; deed.abnf's; date-string and affirm-member are common.abnf's. Requires
; RFC 7405 (%s"..." case-sensitive literals).
;
; Where it applies: INTENT.deed, MUST.deed, TRUST.deed, ADJUST.deed,
; DUST.deed and BUST.deed (head descriptile-deed, J14), at the top level of
; the form. The file name fixes the verb: INTENT.deed is intend (A7 8.1
; table), the others are their own verb. SEMANTIC (validator-enforced,
; deed_lint.js --verb-descriptile):
;   * the form carries :schema-version, :canonical-name (a string) and
;     :of-chora (the repo's version 8 chora id, #uuid or #u8, J20, J28), each exactly
;     once, and no :beholding-chora (J20);
;   * the affirmation members: :affirmed and :affirmed-by exactly once each,
;     :expires at most once and not before :affirmed (J4: required by default;
;     no relaxation can be written until the agentic module and the J19
;     receipt interface exist). Whether :expires is still in the future is the
;     runner's check (YD06), since it depends on the day it runs;
;   * every other top-level member is a verb-fact; no (rule …) (YF02, YL3).

verb-fact       = "(" %s"fact" 1*(token-sep fact-member) [token-sep] ")"
                ; SEMANTIC: :witnesses and :evidence exactly once each, and
                ; no member twice. :witnesses is an A5 name segment
                ; (1*(ALPHA / DIGIT / "." / "_" / "-")), unique in the file
                ; (one fact per rule), and, when the verb's <Verb>file.deed is
                ; read alongside, the :id of one of its rules (YD02, J5).
                ; In INTENT, MUST, TRUST, ADJUST and DUST: :value exactly once,
                ; and no :inherent, :residual or :justification. In BUST:
                ; :inherent and :residual exactly once each, and no :value,
                ; since the residual grade is the fact (8.5).
fact-member     = ( %s":witnesses"     token-sep string )
                / ( %s":evidence"      token-sep evidence )
                / ( %s":value"         token-sep value )
                / ( %s":source"        token-sep string )
                / ( %s":inherent"      token-sep bust-grade )
                / ( %s":residual"      token-sep bust-grade )
                / ( %s":justification" token-sep string )
                ; :source is a repo-relative POSIX path (SEMANTIC: no leading
                ; "/", no "." or ".." segment). A fact never restates the edict
                ; it witnesses (YL3), so there is no :text.

evidence        = %s"draft" / %s"designed" / %s"assumed" / %s"tested"
                / %s"audited" / %s"proven" / %s"measured"
                ; A2 D2: the governance register's six plus measured (YD03).
                ; SEMANTIC: the whole symbol, so "testedx" is refused.

bust-grade      = DQUOTE grade-letter grade-number DQUOTE
grade-letter    = %s"A" / %s"B" / %s"C" / %s"D" / %s"E" / %s"X"
                ; A elimination, B substitution, C prevention, D mitigation,
                ; E accepted, X not investigated (8.5).
grade-number    = %x31-35
                ; 1 devastating to 5 trivial (8.5). A residual "X1" blocks
                ; at the gate (8.5, the estate floor); the profile only
                ; checks the form.
